														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2693052">
									

<p>Antarctica Nazis are always preferable to Illinois Nazis. The ongoing fascination with Third Reich superscience and Wunderwaffe is a strange cultural phenomenon. I blame Pauwels and Bergier; &quot;Morning of the Magicians&quot; introduced an entire generation to it.</p>
<p>This doesn't seem to inspire sympathy for this unlikely and unlikeable AI, at least for me. Unlike a number of other SCPs, this seems too primitive to possess sentience, which is my benchmark for sympathy. The Brave Little Toaster was more of a character.</p>
<p>It does make me wonder what the point of the project was. Human beings can be produced relatively cheaply using unskilled labor, and they already had the Lebensborn homes. Perhaps there was something special about these particular bottle babies?</p>

